[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3547758328","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111714#issuecomment-3547758328","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111714","id":3547758328,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Tdn74","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-18T13:56:43Z","updated_at":"2025-11-18T13:56:43Z","body":"Thank you for your review, AThousandShips! I included your suggested changes into the code!","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3547758328/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3780811007","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111714#issuecomment-3780811007","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111714","id":3780811007,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hWpj_","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-21T19:41:13Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T19:41:13Z","body":"Apparently, SDL only reports pressure values of 0 or 1, so I will probably need to remove the method to get the pressure value, because it's not that useful in this case.\r\n<img width=\"1457\" height=\"457\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5f2b459f-9f0e-41cf-9f7f-49cfcb52e431\" />\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3780811007/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4076794572","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111714#issuecomment-4076794572","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111714","id":4076794572,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7y_vLM","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-17T17:41:24Z","updated_at":"2026-03-17T17:41:24Z","body":"Since this PR lacked a proposal I decided to write one: https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/14481","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4076794572/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4419891825","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111714#issuecomment-4419891825","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111714","id":4419891825,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABB3IycQ","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-11T10:43:12Z","updated_at":"2026-05-11T10:43:12Z","body":"Thank you for your review, bruvzg! :)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4419891825/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4440365873","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111714#issuecomment-4440365873","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111714","id":4440365873,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCKqbMQ","user":{"login":"Birdulon","id":5397662,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzOTc2NjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5397662?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon","html_url":"https://github.com/Birdulon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-13T11:18:14Z","updated_at":"2026-05-13T11:18:14Z","body":"> Apparently, SDL only reports pressure values of 0 or 1, so I will probably need to remove the method to get the pressure value, because it's not that useful in this case. <img alt=\"image\" width=\"1457\" height=\"457\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/92302738/538748353-5f2b459f-9f0e-41cf-9f7f-49cfcb52e431.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..6sa77Vbb15IWiPJpisRWzkqdtbznuotBLpk5v5D_3as\">\r\n\r\nTrue for Sony controllers, however Valve controllers do report a range of pressure values. Tested on Steam Deck Desktop Mode (Gaming Mode forces Steam Input to present an emulated xinput controller) on SDL3 `main`, and the new Steam Controller (codename \"triton\") with https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL/pull/15528\r\n<img width=\"2044\" height=\"1416\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/49a28d11-063e-44c7-96a7-c67b188e24d9\" />\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4440365873/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4458537525","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111714#issuecomment-4458537525","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111714","id":4458537525,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCb_iNQ","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-15T09:15:19Z","updated_at":"2026-05-15T09:15:19Z","body":"Thank you for your review, AThousandShips! :)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4458537525/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4624833563","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111714#issuecomment-4624833563","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111714","id":4624833563,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABE6lcGw","user":{"login":"Birdulon","id":5397662,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzOTc2NjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5397662?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon","html_url":"https://github.com/Birdulon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-04T18:02:08Z","updated_at":"2026-06-04T18:02:08Z","body":"Messing around again now that I have a project to properly use the Steam Controller in. I've put up a branch roughly tracking this one with very hackily backported Steam Controller (2026 \"Triton\") support from SDL 3.4.10 for anyone else with a Steam Controller interested in playing around in the meantime.\r\n\r\nFirst observation for this PR: Zero pressure `SDL_EVENT_GAMEPAD_TOUCHPAD_DOWN` and `SDL_EVENT_GAMEPAD_TOUCHPAD_MOTION` events are legitimate and very desirable. I've patched the logic to not use pressure as a heuristic and instead use `SDL_EVENT_GAMEPAD_TOUCHPAD_UP` to actually release the finger: https://github.com/Birdulon/godot/commit/81c76e9576c839cab925ee069a1f06d4d0cde275\r\nI can't physically obtain a (0,0) touch on my controller but I do have reservations about `Vector2.ZERO` being the guard value for `get_joy_touchpad_finger_position` and `0.0` for `get_joy_touchpad_finger_pressure`. Of course, `get_joy_touchpad_fingers` can be used to confirm that a finger is not being tracked, but there is the technical possibility of (x=0, y=0, pressure=0) being a valid finger state mistakenly treated as absent, and that bothers me.\r\n\r\nSecond observation: `SDL_EVENT_GAMEPAD_TOUCHPAD_UP` could rightly be considered a useful event in and of itself, like releasing a button. I haven't yet tested if it properly includes the coordinates of the release, because...\r\nMaybe instead of only having functions to poll the current state, it could also fire off Events like the computer touchpad does? I know this increases the scope of the PR and could be handled in a future one, but now seems like a good time to talk API decisions.\r\n\r\nThanks @Nintorch for your work on this PR and also on #106218, I really appreciate being able to play around with this stuff and I hope my comments here and elsewhere don't come off as complaining too much!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4624833563/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4624930433","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111714#issuecomment-4624930433","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111714","id":4624930433,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABE6rWgQ","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-04T18:16:39Z","updated_at":"2026-06-04T18:16:39Z","body":"Hello! Thank you for your feedback!\r\n\r\n> First observation for this PR: Zero pressure `SDL_EVENT_GAMEPAD_TOUCHPAD_DOWN` and `SDL_EVENT_GAMEPAD_TOUCHPAD_MOTION` events are legitimate and very desirable. I've patched the logic to not use pressure as a heuristic and instead use `SDL_EVENT_GAMEPAD_TOUCHPAD_UP` to actually release the finger: [Birdulon@81c76e9](https://github.com/Birdulon/godot/commit/81c76e9576c839cab925ee069a1f06d4d0cde275)\r\n\r\nI didn't know it was possible, but in this case I agree that it is a good idea to track presses/releases separately from pressure. I think we can add these features in a separate PR, since this one is already marked as ready to merge for 4.8. 😅 \r\n\r\n> I can't physically obtain a (0,0) touch on my controller but I do have reservations about `Vector2.ZERO` being the guard value for `get_joy_touchpad_finger_position` and `0.0` for `get_joy_touchpad_finger_pressure`. Of course, `get_joy_touchpad_fingers` can be used to confirm that a finger is not being tracked, but there is the technical possibility of (x=0, y=0, pressure=0) being a valid finger state mistakenly treated as absent, and that bothers me.\r\n\r\nGood idea, I think returning `Vector2(-1, -1)` for position and `-1` for pressure would make more sense here.\r\n\r\n> Second observation: `SDL_EVENT_GAMEPAD_TOUCHPAD_UP` could rightly be considered a useful event in and of itself, like releasing a button. I haven't yet tested if it properly includes the coordinates of the release, because... Maybe instead of only having functions to poll the current state, it could also fire off Events like the computer touchpad does? I know this increases the scope of the PR and could be handled in a future one, but now seems like a good time to talk API decisions.\r\n\r\nThis is planned to be done in a separate PR! :)\r\n\r\n> Thanks @Nintorch for your work on this PR and also on #106218, I really appreciate being able to play around with this stuff and I hope my comments here and elsewhere don't come off as complaining too much!\r\n\r\nYou're welcome! And I'm glad my PRs are useful, that means a lot! :) ❤️ ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4624930433/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4632724133","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111714#issuecomment-4632724133","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111714","id":4632724133,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABFCHCpQ","user":{"login":"Birdulon","id":5397662,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzOTc2NjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5397662?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon","html_url":"https://github.com/Birdulon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-05T14:39:17Z","updated_at":"2026-06-05T14:39:17Z","body":"> This PR adds the ability to use touchpads on supported controllers, such as DualShock 4, DualSense ~and (most likely) Steam Deck built-in controls~ (EDIT: apparently not, since \"thirdparty/sdl/joystick/hidapi/SDL_hidapi_steamdeck.c\" file doesn't have any references to touchpads).\r\n\r\nForgot to clarify on this earlier - SDL did get Steam Deck touchpad support after that was written. It requires Steam to not be running, hence my earlier \"only in Desktop Mode\" comment. Desktop Mode with Steam running, and Gaming Mode both hijack the controller (Deck built-in *and* external Steam Controllers!) and make it impossible to access the non-xinput/kbm controls through SDL.\r\nThe only option for Steam games is to use SteamInput API which\r\n1) AFAIK requires license stuff prohibiting it from ever being upstreamed in Godot unless Valve decides to change it, and\r\n2) doesn't let you play with the touchpads or extra buttons directly, just allows you to define \"actions\" that Steam will allow mapping the fancy inputs to *outside* of your game. Your game has the privilege of setting the default mappings, and asking what is mapped to what, so that you can display the correct glyphs, but you don't get to ask what the state of the touchpads or gyroscope or accelerometers are directly, as far as I can tell.\r\n\r\nSo anyone shipping a game on multiple platforms will need to handle the input at least slightly differently for their Steam release (https://godotsteam.com/tutorials/inputs/).\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nRandom use case feedback: I'm finding myself operating on Vector3(x, y, pressure). Convenient for deltas and some 3D input reasoning, but perhaps too niche to consider adding it to the API.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4632724133/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4633931005","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111714#issuecomment-4633931005","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111714","id":4633931005,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABFDQs_Q","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar